From: HeavyGee <gc@lockhouse.systems>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(soup): stop runner sessions serially in the concurrency test

feat/tier-b-reattach-orphan-runner-children serialised the stop loop in
the runner concurrency integration test because parallel /stop-session
under load races the control server and flakes with intermittent HTTP
failures on busy hosts. This host runs ~30 agents, so it is the busy
case. Upstream went back to Promise.all(...map(stopRunnerSession)).

The layer merge takes the base for this file (the base has 13 tests to
the layer's 12, and a richer 'stopped' | 'already_gone' return contract
that the layer's boolean[] would not typecheck against), so the fix is
reapplied here on top of the base contract rather than by taking the
layer side.

It has to be a heal, not a merge resolution: those lines sit OUTSIDE the
conflict region (git treated them as common context), and rerere only
replays conflicted regions, so a hand edit there is silently discarded
by the next compose.

diff --git a/cli/src/runner/runner.integration.test.ts b/cli/src/runner/runner.integration.test.ts
index 7a100916a..baece18fe 100644
--- a/cli/src/runner/runner.integration.test.ts
+++ b/cli/src/runner/runner.integration.test.ts
@@ -662,8 +662,14 @@ if (process.argv[2] === 'runner' && process.argv[3] === 'start-sync') {
       const sessions = await listRunnerSessions();
       expect(sessions).toHaveLength(sessionCount);
 
-      // Stop all sessions
-      const stopResults = await Promise.all(sessionIds.map(sessionId => stopRunnerSession(sessionId)));
+      // Stop serially. Parallel /stop-session under load races the control
+      // server and flakes with intermittent HTTP failures on busy hosts (this
+      // one runs ~30 agents), which is why the fork's tier-b layer serialised
+      // it. The base's richer 'stopped' | 'already_gone' contract is kept.
+      const stopResults: Array<Awaited<ReturnType<typeof stopRunnerSession>>> = [];
+      for (const sessionId of sessionIds) {
+        stopResults.push(await stopRunnerSession(sessionId));
+      }
       expect(stopResults.every(r => r === 'stopped' || r === 'already_gone'), 'Not all sessions reported stopped').toBe(true);
 
       // Verify all sessions are stopped
